&lt;p>Now let&amp;rsquo;s get to the interesting part. The configuration.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="set-up-shared-call-history-for-call-queues">Set up Shared Call History for Call Queues.
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>You&amp;rsquo;ll first need to create a shared call history template in Teams Admin Center. You can decide if all agents with Teams Premium and thus access to the Queues app can see missed or answered calls or if only authorized users should see them. In my case, I chose that agents (that term feels weird now&amp;hellip;) that aren&amp;rsquo;t authorized users can see everything.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-8.png"
width="2249"
height="1635"
srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-8_hu_3aa597bd68868656.png 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-8_hu_a77ab47d143c3954.png 1024w"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Shared call history template"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="137"
data-flex-basis="330px"
>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Next, you&amp;rsquo;ll need to assign the created template to a call queue and save the changes.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-9.png"
width="2249"
height="1635"
srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-9_hu_fb58b98dc0c3b7d3.png 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-9_hu_d6cec8712bec5111.png 1024w"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Shared call history template configuration on a call queue"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="137"
data-flex-basis="330px"
>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>It may take some time until the Queues app reflects the changes and replaces the &lt;strong>Calls&lt;/strong> tab with &lt;strong>Shared calls&lt;/strong>. Only calls received after the template has been assigned to the queue will be shown in shared call history. If you remove the template from the queue again, the tab will revert to &lt;strong>Calls&lt;/strong>.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>After removing the template, I added it back and the previous call history entries were restored. However, calls that were missed when no template is assigned will not be visible. I placed a test call at &lt;code>21:50&lt;/code> while shared call history was disabled and that call is not visible anywhere.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-10.png"
width="2236"
height="1276"
srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-10_hu_3e54a473a5483ae8.png 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-10_hu_f815265a62b2c397.png 1024w"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Call queue where template was removed"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="175"
data-flex-basis="420px"
> &lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-11.png"
width="2236"
height="1276"
srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-11_hu_39c88fdddd22953c.png 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-11_hu_7b6491eb54f89678.png 1024w"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Restored shared call history after re-assigning the template"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="175"
data-flex-basis="420px"
>&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="license-details">License Details
&lt;/h3>&lt;p>The Premium License is only needed to view the shared call history in Teams. It doesn&amp;rsquo;t look like it&amp;rsquo;s required to configure it or for the backend to do its thing. After all, you could also choose &lt;strong>None&lt;/strong> for each of the permissions in a template. More on that later.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="how-does-shared-call-history-work">How Does Shared Call History Work?
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>Let&amp;rsquo;s take a look under the hood, shall we?&lt;/p>
&lt;p>When you assign a shared call history template for a call queue, two special chats are created. One is for &lt;strong>answered&lt;/strong> and the other one for &lt;strong>missed calls&lt;/strong>.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The &lt;code>chatId&lt;/code> looks something like this:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;div class="chroma">
&lt;table class="lntable">&lt;tr>&lt;td class="lntd">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code>&lt;span class="lnt">1
&lt;/span>&lt;span class="lnt">2
&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>
&lt;td class="lntd">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">19:sharedcallqueuelogs_answered_dGVhbXNzdHJlYW1fYW5zd2VyZWRjYWxsbG9nc185MzU3YjMwNS0yOTZlLTRhYzMtODljMS01ZWRlNWJjY2U2NTc=@thread.v2
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">19:sharedcallqueuelogs_missed_dGVhbXNzdHJlYW1fbWlzc2VkY2FsbGxvZ3NfOTM1N2IzMDUtMjk2ZS00YWMzLTg5YzEtNWVkZTViY2NlNjU3@thread.v2
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>&lt;/tr>&lt;/table>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;p>Who would have thunk it but the cryptic looking part is just a Base64 encoded string that includes the call queue&amp;rsquo;s identity. This is the same Id you can get either from PowerShell or copy from the URL in TAC.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-12.png"
width="1984"
height="1210"
srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-12_hu_c8c4d506d753ebfb.png 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-12_hu_6f669c0062e4058.png 1024w"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Decoded Base64 string"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="163"
data-flex-basis="393px"
>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>That means that we can quite easily reconstruct a &lt;code>chatId&lt;/code> by simply knowing a queue&amp;rsquo;s identity.&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;div class="chroma">
&lt;table class="lntable">&lt;tr>&lt;td class="lntd">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code>&lt;span class="lnt">1
&lt;/span>&lt;span class="lnt">2
&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>
&lt;td class="lntd">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma">&lt;code class="language-powershell" data-lang="powershell">&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="nv">$base64EncodedCallQueueId&lt;/span> &lt;span class="p">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="p">[&lt;/span>&lt;span class="no">System.Convert&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">]::&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">ToBase64String&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">([&lt;/span>&lt;span class="no">System.Text.Encoding&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">]::&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">UTF8&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="py">GetBytes&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="s2">&amp;#34;teamsstream_missedcalllogs_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">$(&lt;/span>&lt;span class="nv">$cq&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">.&lt;/span>&lt;span class="n">Identity&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">)&lt;/span>&lt;span class="s2">&amp;#34;&lt;/span>&lt;span class="p">))&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span class="line">&lt;span class="cl">&lt;span class="nv">$chatId&lt;/span> &lt;span class="p">=&lt;/span> &lt;span class="s2">&amp;#34;19:sharedcallqueuelogs_missed_&lt;/span>&lt;span class="nv">$base64EncodedCallQueueId&lt;/span>&lt;span class="s2">@thread.v2&amp;#34;&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>&lt;/tr>&lt;/table>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;p>To get the &lt;code>chatId&lt;/code> of the answered call logs, we simply replace &lt;code>missed&lt;/code> with &lt;code>answered&lt;/code> in the example code above.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Now we can use an Entra app/service principal that has at least the application permission &lt;code>ChatMessage.Read.All&lt;/code> and run &lt;code>Get-MgChatMessage -ChatId {ChatId}&lt;/code>.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-13.png"
width="1734"
height="955"
srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-13_hu_7607e136c1a33dac.png 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-13_hu_a8a68bb3b61f5966.png 1024w"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Output of Get-ChatMessage against shared call history chats"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="181"
data-flex-basis="435px"
>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Note: &lt;code>ChatId&lt;/code> is truncated in the output.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>This will return a message for each call that was logged as either missed or answered. But sadly, Graph doesn&amp;rsquo;t return much data here. All we can get is a &lt;code>callId&lt;/code> in the message body but that doesn&amp;rsquo;t help us much yet since it will take a couple of minutes until that is available in the &lt;a class="link" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/callrecords-callrecord-get?view=graph-rest-1.0&amp;amp;tabs=http" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
>callRecord&lt;/a> Graph endpoint.&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="good-to-know">Good to Know
&lt;/h3>&lt;h4 id="graph-edge-cases">Graph Edge Cases
&lt;/h4>&lt;p>Getting the chat itself via &lt;code>Get-MgChat&lt;/code> failes, even if the app has the &lt;code>Chat.Read.All&lt;/code> permission.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-14.png"
width="1734"
height="955"
srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-14_hu_62e87533547dc840.png 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-14_hu_f262deb403946dee.png 1024w"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Error message for Get-MgChat"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="181"
data-flex-basis="435px"
>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Getting a chat of a call queue that has a template assigned but never received any calls works but returns an empty result. And running the command against a generated &lt;code>chatId&lt;/code> for a call queue that never had a template assigned fails. That&amp;rsquo;s why I said earlier the call log chats are provisioned when you assign a template to a queue for the first time.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-15.png"
width="1734"
height="955"
srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-15_hu_755df7f2366f9797.png 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-15_hu_46b48ee03acddad8.png 1024w"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="Example output of empty and non-existent chats"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="181"
data-flex-basis="435px"
>&lt;/p>
&lt;h4 id="templates-with-no-data-access">Templates with No Data Access
&lt;/h4>&lt;p>If a template is set to &lt;code>None&lt;/code> for incoming and outgoing calls, the calls are still logged in the special call log chats but don&amp;rsquo;t appear in the Queues app. In fact, the Queues app reverts to the standard &lt;strong>Calls&lt;/strong> tab even though the template is still assigned to the queue.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-17.png"
width="2236"
height="1276"
srcset="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-17_hu_6f9905044410dab7.png 480w, https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-17_hu_e223ae77cc793c5a.png 1024w"
loading="lazy"
decoding="async"
alt="No missed calls without permission in template"
class="gallery-image"
data-flex-grow="175"
data-flex-basis="420px"
> &lt;img src="https://heusser.pro/p/exploring-shared-call-history-for-microsoft-teams-call-queues-vrnzevrogniq/image-18.png"
width="1734"
height="955"
